{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/splitnavigation"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftRouting"}],"role":"article","title":"Split Navigation","roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/SplitNavigation"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to implement sidebar-based split navigation with SwiftRouting."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftRouting provides first-class support for ","type":"text"},{"code":"NavigationSplitView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RoutingSplitView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/SplitModel","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". All three columns (sidebar, content, detail) share the same split-type ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — column selection is driven by typed, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values, and only the detail column has a navigation stack, bound directly to that shared router’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"path","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A split-type "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is created automatically and injected into the environment via "},{"code":"@Environment(\\.router)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/SplitModel","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", giving you typed bindings and programmatic selection alongside the regular "},{"code":"push","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"present","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"cover","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" API."}]},{"text":"2-Column Layout (Sidebar + Detail)","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"2-Column-Layout-Sidebar-+-Detail"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The sidebar shows a fixed route; the detail column is derived from a typed selection:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["RoutingSplitView(destination: AppRoute.self, sidebar: .sidebar) { (type: PlayerType) in","    AppRoute.players(type)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"text":"3-Column Layout (Sidebar + Content + Detail)","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"3-Column-Layout-Sidebar-+-Content-+-Detail"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a "},{"code":"content:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure to introduce a middle column. The sidebar drives the content column, and the content column drives the detail column:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["RoutingSplitView(destination: AppRoute.self, sidebar: .sidebar) { (type: PlayerType) in","    AppRoute.players(type)","} detail: { (player: Player) in","    AppRoute.player(player)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Driving Selections","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Driving-Selections"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router\/detailBinding(as:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router\/contentBinding(as:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to wire a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"List"},{"text":" selection directly, or call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router\/select(detail:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router\/select(content:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" programmatically:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct SidebarScreen: View {","    @Environment(\\.router) var router","    let items: [PlayerType] = PlayerType.allCases","","    var body: some View {","        List(items, selection: router.detailBinding(as: PlayerType.self)) { item in","            NavigationLink(item.label, value: item)","        }","        .onFirstAppear {","            guard !router.isCompact else { return }","            router.select(detail: items.first)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router\/hasContentColumn"},{"type":"text","text":" to branch between driving the content or the detail column from the same sidebar code path:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["if router.hasContentColumn {","    router.select(content: playerType)","} else {","    router.select(detail: playerType)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Compact Mode (iPhone)","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Compact-Mode-iPhone"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On iPhone, "},{"code":"NavigationSplitView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" collapses into a single-column stack. Use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router\/isCompact"},{"type":"text","text":" to skip auto-selection and let the user tap to navigate instead:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".onFirstAppear {","    guard !router.isCompact else { return }","    router.select(detail: items.first)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isCompact"},{"text":" reflects ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"horizontalSizeClass"},{"text":", so it also updates during iPad multitasking.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Navigating Within a Column","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Navigating-Within-a-Column"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"router.push(_:)"},{"text":" works like everywhere else in SwiftRouting, but since all columns share the same split ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", it always pushes onto the one navigation stack — rendered only in the detail column. Pushing from the sidebar or content column doesn’t open a stack there; it appears in the detail column instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"router.present(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cover(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are also router-wide, not per-column: calling them from any column presents the same sheet\/cover over the whole "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RoutingSplitView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Deep Linking","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Deep-Linking"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/SplitDeeplinkHandler"},{"text":" to convert an external input into a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/SplitDeeplink"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Router\/handle(splitDeeplink:)"},{"text":" to apply it:","type":